    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable pitching matchups to compensate for the absence of core production from our injured stars. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.39) headlines our lineup, carrying the highest efficiency score of the day. His matchup against Fisher is a \"Strong\" play, bolstered by a significant +14% boost from his dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable SP skill profile. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier is **Drake Baldwin** (69.55), who benefits from a high xwOBA and an aggressive order placement against Rodriguez, and **Heliot Ramos** (62.74), whose ability to exploit Fisher\u2019s slow delivery adds a layer of stolen base potential that remains a critical priority for our roster construction.\n\nWhile **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** face a challenging outing against the high-skill arm of Seymour (xERA 3.34), they remain locked in despite depressed scores. Our most complex decision centered on the outfield, where **Wade Meckler** (59.97) narrowly missed the \"Strong\" threshold but remains a vital piece due to his elite table-setting role and the +19% advantage derived from facing Dobnak. **Miguel Vargas** (52.78) was the closest to a promotion; while his xwOBA of .380 is elite, he was ultimately edged out by the superior platoon and park adjustments afforded to our starting outfielders. We must exercise caution with **Andy Pages** (47.54), as he draws the day\u2019s most difficult assignment against the elite Misiorowski; his start is contingent on his order protection, but he remains our primary candidate to be capped if the game flow trends negative. With **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Luis Robert Jr.** all confirmed unavailable due to injury, the margin for error is thin, making **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s lead-off spot critical to maintaining our category output today.",
